It should keep a //- line comment and a following /- -/ block comment apart (joining them un-comments the block text)
<p>before</p>
//- email_GlobalFooter ]}
/-
This is the global footer, wrapped in a raw tag.

Otherwise, the variables will be populated when you first select the template.

The variables processed per person:
- Person: the current person receiving the email
- campus: to get their campus address
-/
{% raw %}<p>raw</p>{% endraw %}

It should keep consecutive //- line comments on their own lines
<p>x</p>
//- one
//- two
<p>y</p>

It should keep a //- comment on its own line inside an element, before text
<p>
//- note
Hello there
</p>

It should keep text after a trailing //- comment on the next line
<p>Hello //- note
World</p>

It should collapse a short /- -/ block comment onto one line
<div>
/-
short
-/
</div>

It should reindent a multi-line /- -/ block comment
<table><tr><td>
{% if a %}
/- multi
  line -/
<b>x</b>
{% endif %}
</td></tr></table>

It should leave an unterminated /- as text
<p>and/-or text</p>

It should leave dash comments inside quoted attribute values alone
<a title="x //- y /- z -/">link</a>
